                    <Br12 />As a <strong>User Experience Designer (UX Designer)</strong>, I combine a background in <strong>design thinking</strong> and <strong>systemic methodology</strong>, focusing on building <strong>user-centered product experiences</strong> that integrate <strong>research, interaction, and strategic design</strong>.

                    <Br12 />My approach begins with <strong>user research</strong> and <strong>information architecture</strong>, extracting <strong>clarity</strong> from <strong>complex business logic</strong>—making <strong>processes perceptible</strong>, <strong>interfaces understandable</strong>, and <strong>interactions adaptable</strong>.

                    <Br12 />I studied at the <strong>École Nationale Supérieure d’Art de Nancy</strong> (ENSA Nancy) and the <strong>Hubei Institute of Fine Arts</strong> (HIFA), where I learned to shape emotional experiences through visual and spatial thinking.
                    <Br12 />At <strong>Digital Campus Paris</strong>, I developed a structured understanding of <strong>UX strategy and product design frameworks</strong>, learning how to balance <strong>innovation, constraints, and user value</strong> in real-world projects.

                    <Br12 />As a method-driven designer, I consistently pursue <strong>clarity of experience</strong> and <strong>system coherence</strong>, treating every project as a <strong>user-centered laboratory</strong>:

                    <Br8 />Iterating prototypes, testing hypotheses, and validating behaviors,
                    <Br0 />transforming complex systems into <strong>intuitive and fluid experiences</strong>,
                    <Br0 />exploring the synergy between <strong>user journeys</strong>, <strong>information structures</strong>, and <strong>interaction languages</strong>,
                    <Br0 />and grounding every decision in <strong>measurable UX indicators and user feedback</strong>,
                    <Br0 />to ensure each iteration truly enhances <strong>usability and satisfaction</strong>.

                </SectionText>
